					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-438316#post-4329604</guid>
				<title>Excellent Article</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-438316/scp-j#post-4329604</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Tue, 13 Aug 2019 14:56:59 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Copper Dioxide</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>5519772</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>This article is a great insipration for new author, reminding them that even if you do not have skills whatsoever you can still succede as well as reminding them that Effort is not equal to success. Just how SCP-173 might not be a good SCP, but it is a good FIRST SCP ( it's content introcuging the reading to the Foundation world through several clever details such as the fact that there is a secret organization that has delt with anomalies long enough to create Special Containment Procedures and devise safest way of interacting with it and the fact that it's numbers are 173, suggesting there are 172 more of these anomalies) SCP&#8212;J might not be a good SCP, but it is a great insiration for authors. That's a +1 from me</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
